---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/global/Nav.astro";
import AnnouncementBar from "../components/global/AnnouncementBar.astro";
import FooterV2 from "../components/global/FooterV2.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/LegalPage.astro";

const title = "Terms of Use — VistIQ";
const description =
  "The terms governing your use of the VistIQ website: acceptable use, intellectual property, disclaimers, liability and the applicable law.";

/** Bump when the document changes — it drives the "Last updated" line. */
const UPDATED = "2026-08-20";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="/terms-of-use"
  noindex
>
  <main class="main-wrapper">
    <AnnouncementBar />
    <Nav belowAnnouncement />

    <LegalPage
      heading="Terms of Use"
      intro="These terms govern your access to and use of the VistIQ website. Access to the VistIQ platform itself is governed by a separate written agreement."
      updated={UPDATED}
    >
      <h2>1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[WEBSITE DOMAIN]</span
        > (the "Site"), you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do not accept them,
        do not use the Site.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Site is published by <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]</span
        >, a <span class="legal_placeholder">[LEGAL FORM]</span> with share capital
        of <span class="legal_placeholder">[SHARE CAPITAL]</span>, registered at <span
          class="legal_placeholder">[REGISTERED ADDRESS]</span
        > under number <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[COMPANY REGISTRATION NUMBER]</span
        > ("VistIQ", "we", "us"). Publication director: <span
          class="legal_placeholder">[PUBLICATION DIRECTOR]</span
        >. Hosting provider: <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[HOSTING PROVIDER NAME AND ADDRESS]</span
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Relationship to the platform agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms cover the Site only. Use of the VistIQ platform, including
        any trial, pilot or production access, is governed by the separate
        subscription or evaluation agreement signed between VistIQ and the
        customer. Where the two conflict in respect of the platform, that
        agreement prevails.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Permitted use</h2>
      <p>
        We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable and revocable
        right to access the Site for your own information and for legitimate
        business purposes.
      </p>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          use the Site in a way that breaches applicable law or infringes the
          rights of others;
        </li>
        <li>
          attempt to gain unauthorised access to the Site, its servers or any
          connected system;
        </li>
        <li>
          probe, scan or test the vulnerability of the Site without our prior
          written authorisation;
        </li>
        <li>
          scrape, crawl or extract content at a scale that disrupts the Site, or
          use it to build a competing product;
        </li>
        <li>
          introduce malware, or take any action that imposes an unreasonable load
          on our infrastructure;
        </li>
        <li>
          reproduce, distribute or publicly display Site content beyond what
          these terms allow.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may suspend or restrict access to the Site, in whole or in part,
        without notice, if we reasonably believe these terms have been breached.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Site and everything it contains — text, graphics, interfaces, logos,
        illustrations, software and their arrangement — are protected by
        intellectual property law and belong to VistIQ or its licensors. The
        VistIQ name and logo are trademarks of VistIQ and may not be used without
        our prior written consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may view, download and print extracts from the Site for your internal
        business use, provided you keep all proprietary notices intact. No other
        licence is granted, whether express or implied.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Content and accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Content on the Site is provided for general information about our
        products. It does not constitute investment, legal, tax or professional
        advice, and no statement on the Site should be relied on as a
        recommendation to make or refrain from making any investment decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Product descriptions, performance figures and roadmap statements describe
        our current expectations and may change without notice. We make
        reasonable efforts to keep the Site accurate and up to date, but we do
        not warrant that it is complete, current or error-free.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party links and marks</h2>
      <p>
        The Site may link to third-party websites and may display third-party
        names, logos or integrations for identification purposes. Those marks
        remain the property of their respective owners, and their appearance does
        not imply a partnership or endorsement unless stated. We do not control
        third-party sites and accept no responsibility for their content or
        practices.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the Site available, but we provide it "as is" and "as
        available". Access may be interrupted for maintenance, updates or reasons
        beyond our control, and we give no guarantee of uninterrupted or
        error-free access.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, VistIQ shall not be liable for any
        indirect or consequential loss, nor for any loss of profit, revenue, data
        or business opportunity, arising from your use of or inability to use the
        Site. <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[CONFIRM WITH COUNSEL: AGGREGATE LIABILITY CAP AND ANY JURISDICTION-SPECIFIC
          CARVE-OUTS]</span
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be
        excluded or limited under applicable law, including liability for fraud
        or for death or personal injury caused by negligence. If you are a
        consumer, your statutory rights are unaffected.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Personal data collected through the Site is handled as described in our <a
          href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a
        >, which forms part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may amend these terms at any time. The version published on this page
        is the one in force, and the revision date at the top shows when it last
        changed. Continuing to use the Site after a change constitutes acceptance
        of the amended terms.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[GOVERNING LAW, e.g. FRENCH LAW]</span
        >. Any dispute relating to the Site shall be submitted to the exclusive
        jurisdiction of the courts of <span class="legal_placeholder"
          >[COMPETENT COURTS]</span
        >, subject to any mandatory protection available to consumers in their
        country of residence.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href="mailto:[LEGAL EMAIL]"
          ><span class="legal_placeholder">[LEGAL EMAIL]</span></a
        > or through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </LegalPage>

    <FooterV2 />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Baseline only: static prose, no section animation and no reveal guard.
  import { initBaseline } from "../scripts/baseline";
  initBaseline();
</script>
